  "final_text": "Done. I noticed the request was internally inconsistent \u2014 \"25 points\" with phi \"0 to 345 in 25 steps\" doesn't match the standard 15\u00b0-spacing convention (which gives only 24 points over that range) \u2014 so I resolved it by using 25 evenly-spaced phi values from 0\u00b0 to 345\u00b0 (step \u224814.375\u00b0), keeping both the exact point count and the stated range. All 25 points passed preflight (W=1.6 GeV is safely above the 1.486 GeV eta threshold, cos \u03b8*=0 avoids the pole, kinematics fall inside the table coverage). Wrote 3 chunked EXCLURAD input files (10/10/5 points, respecting the Fortran reader's 10-point limit) plus `outcome.json` documenting the fix, all in the working directory."
